-- erwartet: P041
-- The parser ate a `pub` in front of EVERY item and silently dropped it at thirteen kinds.
-- The EBNF carries `[ "pub" ]` at exactly seven. **A visibility word that is accepted and
-- thrown away is worse than one that is rejected**: the reader sees a promise nobody keeps.
--
-- **Since 2026-08-25 it is eleven**, and this probe stood on `pub lock` before that -- one of
-- the four carriers that got the word. *A poison probe that becomes legal through a grammar
-- extension measures nothing from that day on*, and it does not stand out: it goes green
-- because the program is right.
--
-- THIS FILE HAS MOVED TWICE, AND THE SECOND MOVE PROVED THE FIRST
-- --------------------------------------------------------------
-- It then stood on `reason`, with the argument that `reason` carries no `pub` and should get
-- none: *"a named set of numbers lowers to an `enum`, and an `enum` binds no symbol."* **On
-- 2026-09-28 `reason` got the word** (server lane, phase 2), and the argument was not narrowly
-- wrong but wrong at its root: `pub` at an item does not mean "binds a C symbol" here, it means
-- "stands in the EXPORT SET". A `type` binds none either and has carried the word since the
-- first day. What forced it at `reason` was `N038`: an `or R` stands in the SIGNATURE, the
-- signature travels into the `.gabi`, and `R` was the one thing an exported signature could
-- name and not explain -- so **no function with an error channel could leave its module**
-- (`~/gabbro-netz/docs/WAENDE-M1.md`, wall 1; the positive side is `beispiele/167`).
--
-- **The third home is therefore chosen differently: an item with NO NAME.** `concurrent { … }`
-- names bodies and has no name of its own (`ItemArt::name()` answers `None`, and `bindung.rs`
-- says why beside it: *"a `concurrent` set binds no symbol -- it names bodies, and the set
-- itself has no name"*). **What has no name can stand in no interface**, however the grammar
-- grows: an export is a name an importer writes. The two earlier homes of this probe were
-- judgements about what DESERVES `pub`; this one is a judgement about what it can attach to at
-- all.
module gift {

static mut ZAHL_A : u32 in 0 .. 1024 = 0;
static mut ZAHL_B : u32 in 0 .. 1024 = 0;

impl fn lauf_a()
    effects { writes ZAHL_A }
    costs   <= 10 ops
{
    ZAHL_A = 1;
}

impl fn lauf_b()
    effects { writes ZAHL_B }
    costs   <= 10 ops
{
    ZAHL_B = 1;
}

-- **And here it falls.** The set has no name, so a `pub` at it can designate nothing -- and the
-- parser says so instead of swallowing the word.
pub concurrent { lauf_a, lauf_b };

}
